# Which program opens what, as this desktop ships.
#
# The menu hands a line that matched no application to the web, and the guide
# and the settings have links in them. Every one of those asks xdg-open rather
# than naming a browser, so the name is written here once and nothing else on
# the machine holds a second copy of it.
#
# It has to be said. There are three browsers on this device and the desktop
# picks between them by what was installed last, which is not a decision
# anybody made. librewolf is the one the palette was written for; chromium is
# kept for the site that will not work in it and is not the one a link should
# land in.
#
# Here rather than under her own config, because the settings panel writes that
# one and this is the answer it starts from. XDG reads hers first and falls
# back to this, so choosing a browser on the Web tab is a file of her own laid
# over this one, and a machine put back together from the manifest still opens
# a link in something.
[Default Applications]
text/html=librewolf.desktop
x-scheme-handler/http=librewolf.desktop
x-scheme-handler/https=librewolf.desktop
